{"term":"levy","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:50ae9d397f3fcbaab4","definition":"To impose (a tax or fine) to collect monies due, or to confiscate property.","example":"to levy a tax","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["leviable","levier","relevy","unlevied"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/levy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c47c4c00d62772bfe9","definition":"To raise or collect by assessment; to exact by authority.","example":"If they do this […] my ransom, then, / Will soon be levied.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["leviable","levier","relevy","unlevied"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/levy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:27d35599899e7bf708","definition":"To draft someone into military service.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["leviable","levier","relevy","unlevied"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/levy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f51db1f3d9df2dce21","definition":"To raise; to collect; said of troops, to form into an army by enrollment, conscription. etc.","example":"Augustine […] inflamed Ethelbert, king of Kent, to levy his power, and to war against them.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["leviable","levier","relevy","unlevied"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/levy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:755607b42